statement:
You get an array `nums` of `n` positive integers. Count the ways to split it into two arrays `arr1` and `arr2` of non-negative integers, both of length `n`, such that:

- `arr1[i] + arr2[i]` equals `nums[i]` at every index `i`;
- `arr1` never decreases from left to right (`arr1[0] <= arr1[1] <= ...`);
- `arr2` never increases from left to right (`arr2[0] >= arr2[1] >= ...`).

Two splits are different when they differ at some position. Return the number of valid splits modulo `10^9 + 7`.

